## OpenInference records where OpenAI-compatible requests actually go

Source: Arize AI · OpenInference — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/%40arizeai/openinference-instrumentation-openai%404.5.0
Published: 2026-11-14
Channel: github

OpenInference’s OpenAI instrumentation records information about model requests in trace spans, the records of individual operations. Its release addresses a visibility gap: a call through a gateway or self-hosted proxy can have no identifiable model provider, leaving its destination unclear.

The instrumentation now reads the client’s base URL and records its host and port as server.address and server.port. It includes hosts without a recognized provider, so destination evidence remains available when llm.provider cannot be inferred. Only host and port are recorded; URL paths and query parameters are excluded.

Why it matters: For teams routing compatible model calls through gateways: check destination attributes alongside provider attribution when investigating routing.

